% Research focus tags are independent of the discipline tags in keywords.
% understanding-human-ai-collaboration: Understanding human-AI collaboration.
% Human side: what people want, their work and context, and how they collaborate with AI.
% understanding-and-characterizing-llm-behavior: Understanding and characterizing LLM behavior.
% Agent side: how language models behave, reason, generate and respond to steering.
% evaluating-consequences-of-ai: Evaluating consequences of AI.
% Consequences for people: benefits, remaining effort, oversight and meaningful control.
% foundation: Foundations outside the three current research focuses.
% theme_fit: direct = directly studies at least one assigned focus;
% indirect = supports a focus without directly studying it; foundational = foundation only.
% For multi-focus papers, theme_rationale distinguishes direct and indirect connections.
% Consequences include more than productivity; indirect relevance is not a measured effect.

